{#-
  PASS 2b — user prompt for the merge call.

  Available here: partials, seed, n_papers, min_areas, max_areas,
  min_area_papers, max_area_papers, project.
-#}
{{ partials | length }} partial taxonomies were induced over overlapping slices
of the labels from {{ n_papers }} papers.

{% for partial in partials %}
TAXONOMY {{ loop.index }}
{% for area in partial.areas %}
- {{ area.name }}: {{ area.definition }}
  subtopics: {{ area.subtopics | join(", ") }}
{%- if area.absorbs %}
  absorbs: {{ area.absorbs | join(", ") }}
{%- endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% endfor %}
{% if seed %}
REQUIRED AREAS

These must appear in the merged taxonomy, with their names exactly as written:
{% for area in seed.areas %}
- {{ area.name }}{% if area.definition %}: {{ area.definition }}{% endif %}
{%- endfor %}

{% endif %}
Merge these into a single taxonomy of {{ min_areas }}-{{ max_areas }} areas.

Requirements:
- Two areas that describe the same thing under different names become one, with
  the clearer name and a definition covering both.
- An area that appeared in only one partial taxonomy is kept if it is genuinely
  distinct, and folded into its nearest neighbour if it is a fragment.
- absorbs: carry over the raw labels from every partial area you merged in, so
  the provenance survives.
- definition: one sentence saying what belongs in the area and what does not.
- Together the areas must cover everything the partials covered.
